[{"id":75242,"sender_id":703,"sender_full_name":"Alec Rhea","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e00125d56e0b0fd03559b254c9b19117?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/2-limits/near/75242\">#1</a> It seems like there’s some confusion in the definition section of the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/2-limit\">2-limit</a> page – it asserts the existence of a pseudonatural equivalence <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≃</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">C</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K(X,L)\\simeq {\\mathrm{Cat}}^\\mathcal{C}(J,K(X,F-)),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≃</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1646em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9146em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.1362em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathcal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0583em;\">C</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0962em;\">J</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mclose\">))</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span></span></span> but these are hom-categories and not 2-categories themselves so pseudonatural transformations aren’t defined on them. The two obvious routes I see to rectify this are to require the equivalence on the full <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span>-categories instead of the hom-categories, or to promote the hom-categories to discrete <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span>-categories, but I’m not sure which (or if either) is implicitly intended. Any clarification is greatly appreciated.</p>","timestamp":1551893838,"subject":"2-limits","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":75248,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/2-limits/near/75248\">#2</a> <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Cat}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span></span></span></span> is a 2-category, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Cat}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span></span></span></span>-valued (hom-)functors have pseudonatural transformations between them.  Perhaps the confusing part is that <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span></span></span></span> is the argument of the functors, i.e. the equivalence is “pseudonatural in <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span></span></span></span>”?</p>","timestamp":1551920952,"subject":"2-limits","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":75250,"sender_id":703,"sender_full_name":"Alec Rhea","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e00125d56e0b0fd03559b254c9b19117?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/2-limits/near/75250\">#3</a> Ah – the part confusing me was how a pseudonatural equivalence could have <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K(X,L)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> (the hom category) as a domain if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span> is just a <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span>-category with hom <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>-categories, but if I understand you correctly this is actually the representable 2-presheaf <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>:</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K(-,L):K\\to {\\mathrm{Cat}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Cat</span></span></span></span></span></span> at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span></span></span></span> on the left and we’re asserting a pseudonatural equivalence to another pseudofunctor?</p>","timestamp":1551928917,"subject":"2-limits","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":75253,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/2-limits/near/75253\">#4</a> Right.</p>","timestamp":1551944533,"subject":"2-limits","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":75254,"sender_id":703,"sender_full_name":"Alec Rhea","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e00125d56e0b0fd03559b254c9b19117?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/2-limits/near/75254\">#5</a> Much appreciated Mike :^).</p>","timestamp":1551957918,"subject":"2-limits","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":84196,"sender_id":777,"sender_full_name":"DELETED_USER_2018","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f0f11e7644eabbad93af93540b759720?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/2-limits/near/84196\">#6</a> [deleted]</p>","timestamp":1592362306,"subject":"2-limits","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":84211,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/2-limits/near/84211\">#7</a> Yes.  There are really only two basic notions of limit that include all the others as special cases: weighted 2-limits and weighted bilimits.  Weighted 2-limits are 2-functorial and weighted bilimits are pseudofunctorial.</p>","timestamp":1592409037,"subject":"2-limits","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":84212,"sender_id":777,"sender_full_name":"DELETED_USER_2018","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f0f11e7644eabbad93af93540b759720?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/2-limits/near/84212\">#8</a> [deleted]</p>","timestamp":1592419441,"subject":"2-limits","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":84224,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/2-limits/near/84224\">#9</a> Have you looked at the references on the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/2-limit\">2-limit</a> page?  Particularly Steve Lack’s <em>2-categories companion</em> is a good overview.</p>","timestamp":1592491179,"subject":"2-limits","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":84229,"sender_id":777,"sender_full_name":"DELETED_USER_2018","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f0f11e7644eabbad93af93540b759720?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/2-limits/near/84229\">#10</a> [deleted]</p>","timestamp":1592518053,"subject":"2-limits","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]}]